  "scientific_notes": [
    "D_lambda=L[(1-lambda)g_global I+lambda diag(g_local)]L with L=D0^(1/2), lambda in [0,1] and rho=2/3 preserves D0/3<=D_lambda<=D0 in PSD order, unchanged storage and quadratic velocity dissipation. The local tangent includes both velocity and angle variations with the correct projected acceleration sign.",
    "The weak equation uses the spatial-minus-global force direction and the same memory projector. Raw lambda is the train cross statistic divided by positive curvature; clipping to [0,1] gives the exact convex one-dimensional optimum. Both raw and clipped values must recover the known endpoint to0.001.",
    "The trace-matched isotropic control uses sum_i (D0)_ii*g_i / tr(D0), separating spatial allocation from a change in total damping. In positive truth, train and val must each beat both controls by the registered residual ratio and numerical-floor margin.",
